const discography=document.querySelector('#discography');if(discography){discography.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin',`<section class="section bio" id="about"><p class="chapter">03 / SAM 101</p><div class="split"><h2>THE LAD<br><em>BEHIND THE NOISE.</em></h2><p class="lead">North Shields made the stories. A guitar, a pub and a chance encounter carried them outward.</p></div><div class="bio-grid"><aside class="bio-facts"><div><span>Full name</span><b>Samuel Thomas Fender</b></div><div><span>Born</span><b>25 April 1994</b></div><div><span>Home</span><b>North Shields, England</b></div><div><span>Voice</span><b>High tenor · Geordie accent</b></div><div><span>First guitar</span><b>Age eight</b></div><div><span>Writing songs</span><b>From age fourteen</b></div></aside><article class="bio-story"><h3>Built in North Shields</h3><p>Sam grew up in a working-class musical family near the mouth of the River Tyne. His father Alan played guitar and piano, while his older brother Liam played drums and introduced him to Jeff Buckley and Bruce Springsteen.</p><p>He learned guitar young, played Hendrix and Kings of Leon covers with childhood friend Dean Thompson, and began writing his own songs as a teenager. Home life, money, friendship, masculinity, grief and the North East became the raw material he still writes from.</p><div class="bio-quote">Local detail. Universal feeling. No costume required.</div><h3>Found behind the bar</h3><p>After school, Sam worked jobs including pulling pints at North Shields’ Low Lights Tavern. Encouraged to fetch his guitar and perform, he was seen there by Owain Davies—Ben Howard’s manager—who took him on. Years of development followed before “Play God” arrived in 2017 and the BRITs Critics’ Choice win accelerated everything in 2019.</p></article></div><section class="band"><h3>The band around Sam</h3><p>The live and recording family has grown with the stages. Roles can shift between songs and tours.</p><div class="band-grid"><article><b>Dean Thompson</b><span>GUITAR · VOCALS · MANDOLIN</span></article><article><b>Drew Michael</b><span>DRUMS · PERCUSSION</span></article><article><b>Joe Atkinson</b><span>KEYS · SYNTHS</span></article><article><b>Tom Ungerer</b><span>BASS</span></article><article><b>Johnny “Blue Hat” Davis</b><span>SAXOPHONE</span></article><article><b>Mark Webb</b><span>GUITAR · LIVE BAND</span></article><article><b>Brooke Bentham</b><span>GUITAR · VOCALS</span></article><article><b>Sam Fender</b><span>VOICE · GUITAR · PIANO</span></article></div></section><section class="gear"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE CORE SOUND</p><div class="gear-name">Fender<br><em>Jazzmaster</em></div></div><div><h3>What he plays</h3><p>Sam’s signature stage guitar is the Fender American Professional Jazzmaster, commonly paired with a Fender Twin amplifier. He favors the Jazzmaster’s bright Fender attack with extra body and warmth—the scale and shimmer behind those wide-open chords.</p><ul><li>Fender American Professional Jazzmaster</li><li>Fender Twin amplifier</li><li>Electric and acoustic guitars across the records</li><li>Piano, organ, harmonica and glockenspiel in the studio</li></ul></div></section><section class="year-now"><h3>2026 so far</h3><div class="now-line"><article><time>FEB 2026</time><b>First UK Number 1 single</b><p>“Rein Me In” completes a record 36-week climb to the summit.</p></article><article><time>FEB 2026</time><b>Two BRIT wins</b><p>Alternative/Rock Act, plus Song of the Year with Olivia Dean.</p></article><article><time>MAY 2026</time><b>O2 surprise</b><p>Sam joins Olivia during her London run to perform “Rein Me In.”</p></article><article><time>MAY 2026</time><b>Ivor Novello</b><p>Named Songwriter of the Year.</p></article><article><time>JUL–AUG</time><b>UK chart history</b><p>“Rein Me In” passes a 73-year record and reaches 21 non-consecutive weeks at Number 1.</p></article><article><time>AUG 1</time><b>Lollapalooza</b><p>Sam and Olivia perform the song together in America for the first time.</p></article></div></section><section class="live-archive" id="live"><div class="archive-head"><div><h3>The live archive is next</h3><p>This area is ready to grow into a show-by-show database: every tour, date, venue, city, country, setlist, encore, guest appearance and source link.</p></div><span class="archive-status">COMING NEXT</span></div><div class="archive-fields"><span>Tour &amp; year</span><span>Date &amp; venue</span><span>Complete setlist</span><span>Guests &amp; notes</span></div></section><p class="info-source">SOURCES: OFFICIAL CHARTS · NEWCASTLE UNITED · ROLLING STONE UK · MUSICRADAR · PREMIER GUITAR · RELEASE CREDITS</p></section>`);}
const lolla=document.querySelector('.lolla-feature');if(lolla){const feature=document.createElement('div');feature.className='lolla-feature lolla-video-feature';feature.innerHTML='<div class="lolla-video"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Q9o_T6BND28" title="Sam Fender and Olivia Dean performing Rein Me In at Lollapalooza" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><span><small>LOLLAPALOOZA</small><strong>Lollapalooza surprise</strong><p>Watch Sam and Olivia perform “Rein Me In” together live.</p><a href="https://youtu.be/Q9o_T6BND28" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Watch on YouTube ↗</a></span>';lolla.replaceWith(feature);}
const toonSection=document.querySelector('#toon');if(toonSection&&!document.querySelector('.artists-on-sam'))toonSection.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin',`<section class="section artists-on-sam" id="artists-on-sam"><p class="chapter">06 / ARTISTS ON SAM</p><div class="artists-heading"><h2>THEY HEAR<br><em>IT TOO.</em></h2><p>New voices and rock legends on Sam’s songs, sound and future.</p></div><div class="artist-voices"><article><small>NEW GENERATION</small><h3>Noah Kahan</h3><blockquote>“It was everything I loved about a song.”</blockquote><p>After hearing “Dead Boys,” Noah restarted it and listened four more times. They later recorded “Homesick.”</p><a href="https://www.facebook.com/noahkahanmusic/posts/940636104096606/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SOURCE ↗</a></article><article><small>NEW GENERATION</small><h3>Benson Boone</h3><blockquote>“He’s an artist I admire… with incredible talent.”</blockquote><p>Benson honored Sam by covering “Seventeen Going Under” at Montreux in 2025.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rAnWNRmrFqA" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">WATCH ↗</a></article><article><small>NEW GENERATION</small><h3>Olivia Dean</h3><blockquote>“I think this is a beautiful song.”</blockquote><p>Her “Rein Me In” verse turned Sam’s song into a two-sided conversation.</p><a href="https://www.musicradar.com/artists/every-time-i-play-a-les-paul-or-anything-i-just-wanna-do-like-ac-dc-sam-fender-releases-behind-the-scenes-footage-of-him-working-on-a-guitar-part-for-rein-me-in-his-hit-single-with-olivia-dean" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SOURCE ↗</a></article><article class="legend"><small>ROCK LEGEND</small><h3>Elton John</h3><blockquote>“They’re so good and they give you so much adrenaline.”</blockquote><p>Elton said “Dead Boys” was so good he practically stopped his car.</p><a href="https://www.nme.com/news/music/elton-john-praises-sam-fender-and-christine-the-queens-they-encourage-you-to-do-better-things-2706709" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SOURCE ↗</a></article><article class="legend"><small>ROCK LEGEND</small><h3>Lindsey Buckingham</h3><blockquote>“He deserves it.”</blockquote><p>He praised the writing in “People Watching” and recognized something of his own guitar language.</p><a href="https://www.musicradar.com/artists/it-did-occur-to-me-that-the-guitar-part-was-very-much-something-i-would-do-lindsey-buckingham-spots-something-familiar-in-a-hit-sam-fender-song-as-he-addresses-how-it-could-have-been-influenced-by-fleetwood-mac" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SOURCE ↗</a></article><article class="legend"><small>GEORDIE LEGENDS</small><h3>Brian Johnson + Mark Knopfler</h3><blockquote>“We both like everything about him.”</blockquote><p>The AC/DC and Dire Straits icons welcomed Sam into their shared North East musical lineage.</p><a href="https://direstraitsblog.com/blog/exclusive-qa-mark-knopfler-brian-johnson-sam-fender/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SOURCE ↗</a></article></div><p class="artists-note"><b>Bruce Springsteen:</b> Sam opened for Bruce in Ferrara and Rome in 2023. No verified direct Bruce quote about Sam has been added. A reliable Mick Jagger comment has not been located, so the site does not attribute one to him.</p></section>`);
